## Key Notes on Sourcing & Data Gaps

**Statutory (IGAAP) line items** — GWP, NWP, NEP, PAT, EoM ratio, Claims ratio, Commission ratio, Combined ratio, Solvency ratio, Net worth, AUM, and Investment yield were all pulled directly from the statutory IRDAI-format **Audited Financial Statements & Management Report** (Revenue Account Schedules 1D/2D/3D/4, Balance Sheet Schedules 5–14, and Annexures 2 & 3 to Schedule 16). This is the correct 1/n-basis statutory full-year filing for FY24 (year ended 31 March 2024) — no H1/9M figures were substituted.

**PAT (IFRS)** was sourced from the audited **IND AS 117 proforma financial statements** (dated 2025-06-25) — ₹1,10,343 Lakh = ₹1,103.43 Cr. Note that the June-2024 Corporate/Analyst Presentation had shown a preliminary/indicative IFRS PAT of ~₹1,080 Cr for FY24 in its "IFRS PnL" bridge slide; this was a pre-finalization estimate. The audited Ind AS 117 proforma figure (₹1,103.43 Cr) is used here as the more authoritative, final statutory number, consistent with the source-hierarchy principle (audited filings > investor presentations).

**Items left blank (not fabricated/estimated):**
- **Retail health GWP** and **Retail health market share** — The Corporate Presentation contains a chart titled "Retail health GWP (Cr) & Market share," but the actual figures are embedded purely as an image with no extractable text/OCR values in the retrieved content. The only extractable GWP figures were company-total GWP (₹15,254.45 Cr, statutory) and industry-ranking figures (~₹15,251 Cr, rounded, per GI Council data) — neither is a true "retail-only" breakout, so neither was substituted.
- **Claims ratio (IFRS)** — Not published as a discrete, explicitly labelled ratio in the IND AS proforma statements.
- **Expense ratio (IGAAP, standalone)** — Only "Expense of Management" ratio variants (to GDP / to NWP) are disclosed; no separately labelled "Expense ratio" line item exists in the statutory filing.</ans>
